  "answer_to_user": "EV / Electrification & Mobility theme, last two weeks (14d), ranked by news attention — with each name's sentiment:\n\n- Tesla (TSLA) — by far the most-covered, 64 items, net-POSITIVE but heavily contested (47 pos / 16 neg): robotaxi momentum offset by a ~3M-vehicle China recall.\n- Energy Absolute (EA.BK) — 15 items, all POSITIVE: arranged 9.8B baht credit to fund an electric-bus project.\n- Hyundai (005380.KO) — 13, POSITIVE: 100+ model product offensive.\n- XPeng (9868.HK) — 10, POSITIVE on balance but with a notable NEG driver (Q3 revenue guide missed consensus by ~15%, stock sank 7%).\n- BYD (002594.CS) — 10, net-positive (July production/sales up YoY) but mixed.\n- Toyota (7203.JP) — 10, net-NEGATIVE: new CEO guides operating margin down to 6.3% by FY2027 — a clear case where high attention is NOT positive.\n- NEX (NEX.BK) 10 pos; Isuzu (7267.JP) 9 pos (record Q1 op profit); Ford (F) 9 pos (fair-value raised); GM 8 pos (restarted Ohio battery output); CATL (300750.CS) 7 pos (+42% profit); LG Energy Solution (373220.KO) 7 pos (Lansing plant); ATP30 (ATP30.BK) 7 pos.\n- Stellantis (STLA.US) — 6, net-NEGATIVE (new Cherokee/STLA One platform read negatively).\n- Volkswagen (VOW.XETRA) — 5, net-positive but CEO warns on margins.\n\nOverall split: 13 of 15 net-positive, 2 net-negative (Toyota, Stellantis). Key nuance: attention volume ≠ sentiment — Tesla and XPeng carry meaningful negative counts, and Toyota is the biggest name whose heavy coverage is actually negative (margin guide-down)."
